bike-share.comment:
I support exploring a transition to a more accessible and affordable municipal bike-share model, including lower-cost non-electric bicycles and affordable membership options.

A successful bike-share system should serve a broad range of residents, including seniors, families, students and people who may not feel comfortable using e-scooters. Providing seated, non-electric bicycles would give residents more transportation choices and improve accessibility.

I would also like to see the Region evaluate the system based on actual usage, cost, safety and community needs. If public funding is involved, we should ensure that the model provides good value for taxpayers while remaining affordable for users.

Other improvements I would consider include:

Better integration with ION and bus transit;
Convenient bike-share stations near major destinations, schools, community facilities and trails;
Secure and accessible bicycle parking;
A range of bicycle options suitable for different ages and abilities; and
Regularly reviewing usage data and resident feedback to adjust the system and improve utilization.

My goal would be a bike-share system that is affordable, accessible, practical and well-used, rather than simply having more shared vehicles on the street.
